  "comment": "We can use the dig command on the localhost of the DNS server to query the ENUM entries, for example, $ dig NAPTR 0.0.0.2.5.2.6.e164.id @127.0.0.1 The output would be approximately ; &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; DiG 9.6.1-P1 &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; NAPTR 0.0.0.2.5.2.6.e164.id @127.0.0.1 ;; global options: +cmd ;; Got answer: ;; -&gt;&gt;HEADER&lt;&lt;- opcode: QUERY, status: NOERROR, id: 10744 ;; flags: qr aa rd ra; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 1, AUTHORITY: 1,",
